# Rust
/target/
crates/**/target/
crates/**/Cargo.lock
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Language bindings — each is a standalone Cargo package with its own
# target/ dir, plus NAPI-rs / maturin generated artifacts. Source files
# under bindings/**/src/, bindings/**/tests/, the manifests, and the
# READMEs are committed; everything else is build output.
bindings/**/target/
# bindings/{acdp-py,acdp-node,acdp-wasm}/Cargo.lock are deliberately
# TRACKED (not ignored): each binding is a standalone Cargo workspace whose
# output is a published application artifact (a compiled wheel / .node /
# .wasm, `publish = false`), not a library — for a cryptographic verifier
# the exact resolved dependency graph is part of what a consumer trusts,
# so the lockfile is committed and every binding build runs `--locked`
# against it. bindings/interop/ has no Cargo.toml of its own, so no
# fourth lockfile is expected here. Each binding's lock resolves
# independently of the root Cargo.lock by design (separate workspaces);
# see ASSUMPTIONS.md for the accepted divergence this produces.
# bindings/acdp-node/package-lock.json is tracked for the same reason:
# napi build's generated loader (index.js/index.d.ts, see below) is
# produced by @napi-rs/cli, so the resolved npm dependency graph is part
# of what a consumer of this application artifact trusts. `npm install`
# (not `npm ci` — see ASSUMPTIONS.md for why that is not viable here) is
# what every binding target runs against it, and it honors a committed
# lock: it will not upgrade an entry that still satisfies its range, so
# the tracked lock is what keeps the pinned @napi-rs/cli version real.
bindings/acdp-py/.venv/
bindings/acdp-py/*.so
bindings/acdp-py/dist/
bindings/acdp-node/node_modules/
# index.js + index.d.ts are the napi-generated loader/type defs. They are
# committed (not ignored) because the bindings-release publish job does not
# run `napi build`, so the root `acdp` package needs them present at publish
# time. Regenerate with `npm run build` after any change to the exported API.
bindings/acdp-node/acdp.*.node
# acdp-wasm: the wasm-pack / wasm-bindgen output dir (.js/.wasm/.d.ts) is
# generated on demand by `wasm-pack build`, never committed.
bindings/acdp-wasm/pkg/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

